## Summary
The article debunks the racist notion that elite institutions routinely hire 'A-minus Black faculty,' which perpetuates stereotypes of Black intellectual inferiority. It argues that this idea is baseless and harmful, and urges readers to reject such racist hype.

## Key Points
- The concept of 'A-minus Black faculty' hiring is a racist stereotype without basis.
- This notion undermines the intellectual capabilities of Black individuals in academia.
- Readers are encouraged to disbelieve and challenge such racist ideas.
- It highlights broader issues of racism and discrimination in elite academic institutions.


